tape_transcript = "Mount Hale Observatory. October 14, 1974. Dr. Thorne recording. The return beam from the Apollo array has stabilized into an active optical conduit. Shadow silhouettes are moving along the floor line. Direct illumination slows them, but they absorb raw forward light. To dissipate them, the beam must be reflected—the phase shift of a mirrored reflection destabilizes their silhouette structure. If the cleanroom interlock engages, use the Argon-ion laser wavelength: 488. Four, eight, eight."

